MIOpen (pinned tag rocm-6.4.4): reject grouped/depthwise convolutions in
ConvOclDirectFwd's applicability check, so MIOpen never selects it (or its
fused variant, ConvOclDirectFwdFused -> MIOpenConvUniBatchNormActiv) for
them on gfx803.

WHY
---
MIOpenConvUniBatchNormActiv (src/kernels/MIOpenConvDirBatchNormActiv.cl,
generated by ConvOclDirectFwd/ConvOclDirectFwdFused,
src/solver/conv/conv_ocl_dir2Dfwd.cpp) does an out-of-bounds read on its
weights buffer for grouped convolutions -- confirmed on real gfx803
hardware (RX 470, ROCm 6.4.4) via a minimal, deterministic, standalone
MIOpen repro (K=240 depthwise 3x3, groups=240, no ORT/model involved) that
reliably faults on the very first execute. Root cause narrowed via
AMD_SERIALIZE_KERNEL=3 (forces synchronous per-kernel execution, so a GPU
page fault attributes to the exact kernel causing it instead of whichever
kernel happened to be in flight when the fault surfaced) -- two
independent captures of the real production crash (CLAP audio-encoder
session churn) both attribute to this exact kernel, with the fault address
landing 69KB-1.1MB past the end of the legitimately-allocated weights
buffer depending on layer size. This is a genuine buffer overrun, not
stale/uninitialized data.

ConvOclDirectFwd::IsApplicable has a filter-size restriction gate that
only applies `if (problem.GetGroupCount() == 1)` -- grouped convolutions
skip that gate entirely and fall through to the final combined condition
with no size/shape restriction specific to groups, reaching the same
broken kernel that non-grouped convs use, without its own group-aware
bounds correctness ever having been established.

WHAT
----
Reject GroupCount() != 1 outright in IsApplicable, so MIOpen routes
grouped convs (fused or not) to a different solver instead. This is
scoped to grouped convolutions only -- non-grouped shapes that
legitimately want this solver are unaffected, unlike the blanket
MIOPEN_DEBUG_CONV_DIRECT_OCL_FWD=0 env var this patch replaces (see
KERNEL_BUGS.md for why that blunter fix was tried first and what this one
improves on).

Applies to: MIOpen @ rocm-6.4.4, gfx803 only -- not upstreamed, this
platform is abandoned; see conv-direct-fwd-grouped-oob.sh for how this
patch is applied and verified at build time.

diff --git a/src/solver/conv/conv_ocl_dir2Dfwd.cpp b/src/solver/conv/conv_ocl_dir2Dfwd.cpp
--- a/src/solver/conv/conv_ocl_dir2Dfwd.cpp
+++ b/src/solver/conv/conv_ocl_dir2Dfwd.cpp
@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@
         && (problem.GetBackwardPadW() < 0 || problem.GetBackwardPadH() < 0))
         return false;

+    // CONV_DIRECT_FWD_GROUPED_OOB_PATCH: MIOpenConvUniBatchNormActiv has an
+    // out-of-bounds weights-buffer read for grouped convolutions on gfx803,
+    // confirmed via a minimal standalone repro and two independent
+    // AMD_SERIALIZE_KERNEL=3-attributed production crashes. This solver's own
+    // filter-size gate below only applies when GroupCount()==1, so grouped
+    // convs reach the broken kernel with no group-aware check at all. Reject
+    // them outright instead. See patches/miopen/conv-direct-fwd-grouped-oob.sh.
+    if(problem.GetGroupCount() != 1)
+        return false;
+
     // Factored out from ConvolutionDescriptor::IsDirectSupported(), which is now dissmissed:
     if (problem.GetGroupCount() == 1)
     {
